  "answer": "No past ticket reports this exact problem: Peek (PowerToys.Peek.UI.exe) started from the command line with a non-existent runner PID shows no UI and stays running as a zombie process until it is ended in Task Manager. The closest ticket, PowerToys#41722, describes the same root cause in Awake: the PID is not validated and WaitForPowerToysRunner is called with a failed OpenProcess handle. That is a different component and symptom, so it is not a match. The only workaround the archive suggests is to end the process in Task Manager and to pass a valid PID, or to launch Peek through PowerToys itself rather than by hand. Please keep this ticket open so that Peek's PID validation can be tracked separately."
